  <item>
    <title>Beaufort County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/beaufort-county-nc</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-beaufort-county-nc</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Commissioners voted 6-1 on Oct 5, 2026 for a one-year moratorium on accepting, processing or approving applications/permits for data centers. Formal vote had been postponed from Sep 14 (informal hearing only). Effective date not stated and no ordinance text read, so end date not computed. No data center currently proposed.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Raleigh: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/raleigh-nc</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-raleigh-nc</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>City Council approved a six-month pause on approvals for large (major-utility) data centers, 7-1 (Christina Jones opposed, saying six months was too short). Vote dated Oct 6 (Tuesday) per WUNC/Axios published Oct 7. End date Apr 6, 2027 is from the city&#x27;s own schedule (&#x27;Council takes final action on draft text amendments; moratorium ends&#x27;). News reports describe scope as roughly 10,000+ sq ft / over 5 MW; the city page gives no thresholds. Ordinance text not read.</description>
  </item>
